   "key": "what_exists",
   "title": "What already exists",
   "text": "The Canadian Society for Mucopolysaccharide & Related Diseases Inc., a patient group based in Canada, is linked to GM2 AB variant in the atlas [E61905c2]. The National Tay-Sachs & Allied Diseases Association, a patient group based in the United States, is also linked to GM2 AB variant [Ed912a71]. A completed trial tested the medicine miglustat in children with juvenile GM2 gangliosidosis, with a study site in Canada [Ec8e5090, E9f76fd6, Ee868ceb, E1d2e970]. A completed natural history study, run by Idorsia Pharmaceuticals Ltd., followed children with early-onset GM1 gangliosidosis, GM2 gangliosidosis, or Gaucher disease type 2, with sites in several countries [E2bbdda4, E5a0d41e]. A registry called 'Registry Gangliosidoses' for GM2 AB variant is based in Germany and run by SphinCS Lyso Gemeinnutzige UG, though its current status is listed as unknown [E5c45a48, E1de801c]. For Tay-Sachs, a related disease, the Cure and Action for Tay-Sachs (CATS) Foundation runs a patient registry called the Tay-Sachs and Sandhoff Disease Registry [E624aa7e, Eb51957b]. For Krabbe, a related disease, NIH NINDS funds a research grant called 'CGT and ACD Inhibitors for SRT Treatment of Krabbe Disease' [E50bb630, Ef352296].",
